# Security & Configuration

## Environment Variables
- `.env*` files are gitignored; Turbo `build` task declares `.env*` as inputs
- `OPENAI_API_KEY` — required by `OpenAIEmbedder` in `@repo/memory`; read from `process.env`
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` — web dashboard API base (defaults to `http://localhost:4000`)

## Secrets Handling
- No secrets in source — `.env*`, `*.pem` are gitignored
- `OpenAIEmbedder` accepts key via constructor options or `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY`
- Never log or persist API keys in event payloads or `EventLog` rows

## Data Storage (gitignored)
- SQLite database: `apps/backend/data/farm.db` (via Prisma, `apps/backend/data/` gitignored)
- Runtime memory: `.bot-ville/` at repo root (JSON files for knowledge, agent state, history)
- JSON fields in SQLite stored as strings; PrismaAdapter serializes/deserializes

## API Security
- `/api/*` routes — full mutation access (intended for desktop app only)
- `/public/*` routes — enforces GET-only (returns 405 on non-GET), used by web dashboard
- No authentication layer currently — security boundary is route prefix separation
- CORS enabled via `@fastify/cors` on the backend

## Electron Security
- Context isolation enabled — renderer cannot access Node.js APIs directly
- `contextBridge` preload exposes a limited `electronAPI` surface
- Exposed methods: `openDirectoryDialog()`, `getWebDashboardInfo()`, IPC send/on/invoke

## Agent Isolation
- Each spawned agent runs in its own git worktree (`WorktreeManager`)
- Agent sessions track `pid`, `workingDirectory`, and `status`
- `AgentSpawner.kill()` terminates agent processes; `prune()` cleans up stale sessions

## Commands
- `pnpm db:push` — push Prisma schema to SQLite (dev)
- `pnpm db:studio` — open Prisma Studio for DB inspection
